  "unit_reviews": [
    {
      "source_interface": "F1",
      "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Probability.GaussianPolynomialRidgeSmooth.standard_gaussian_polynomial_ridge_L2_smooth",
      "kind": "theorem",
      "source_comparison": "accept",
      "module_comparison": "accept",
      "reader_exposition": "accept",
      "dependency_metadata": "accept",
      "reason": "The private induction quantifies over every finite q>=1 and increases q to 2q at the successor. Gaussian projection moments supply the literal linear map into L^(2q); finite-dimensionality of the parameter space makes that linear map continuous. Holder multiplication is L^(2q) x L^(2q) -> L^q, with its HolderTriple exhibited. Constants, polynomial sums and scalar multiples preserve C-infinity. Finally a.e. representative equality transfers membership and Lp.ext identifies the constructed map with the literal toLp map. No unit-vector premise or numerical derivative bound is inserted.",
      "source_interface_canonical_sha256": "eb3fe5c8674ec2449556c2273f16287d430d0bead0d30a3ddc51f055c671dc15",
      "reader_unit_canonical_sha256": "1f031f551eee4f80d01c8a97b189af0ccb7f585ee472a5bc7cff139d51cdec13",
      "reader_steps": 3
    },
    {
      "source_interface": "F2",
      "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Probability.GaussianHermiteFeatures.gaussianHermiteRidgeL2",
      "kind": "def",
      "source_comparison": "accept",
      "module_comparison": "accept",
      "reader_exposition": "accept",
      "dependency_metadata": "accept",
      "reason": "The body maps the integer Hermite polynomial to real coefficients, applies the actual ridge membership witness at w, and calls toLp on that exact literal function. Classical.choose selects a membership-proof family, not an arbitrary feature vector. Membership proofs live in Prop; proof irrelevance, or equivalently toLp representative extensionality, prevents the value of the L2 class from depending on that proof choice. This definition carries no independent theorem credit.",
      "source_interface_canonical_sha256": "8244cecf1e0791e8fe2498432368f999358529684384e6eda861e39d85eed1ef",
      "reader_unit_canonical_sha256": "f2d43773518f1d4780011011529523c3f50f59bab9969eda9220f41f0de4e5b6",
      "reader_steps": 1
    },
    {
      "source_interface": "F3",
      "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Probability.GaussianHermiteFeatures.finiteGaussianHermiteRidgeL2",
      "kind": "def",
      "source_comparison": "accept",
      "module_comparison": "accept",
      "reader_exposition": "accept",
      "dependency_metadata": "accept",
      "reason": "The body is precisely the finite scalar sum of the preceding classes in the same L2 carrier. It allows empty support, arbitrary natural degrees including zero, and signed or zero real coefficients. It assumes neither evenness nor coefficient mass. Empty support gives the zero class.",
      "source_interface_canonical_sha256": "a859b1c88553feaa86a881a5aa247960ae0f00e308d5ddc28269272dab07dec1",
      "reader_unit_canonical_sha256": "d431ba33727d2574866d14130ac42815bf9cf22b0f3174f76b9aa5efa395f0a9",
      "reader_steps": 1
    },
    {
      "source_interface": "F4",
      "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Probability.GaussianHermiteFeatures.gaussianHermiteRidgeL2_contDiff",
      "kind": "theorem",
      "source_comparison": "accept",
      "module_comparison": "accept",
      "reader_exposition": "accept",
      "dependency_metadata": "accept",
      "reason": "The proof specializes the smoothness theorem to the exact real coefficient image used in the definition, takes the property of the same chosen membership witness, and lowers C-infinity to C2. This is global ambient regularity, not only regularity along the sphere.",
      "source_interface_canonical_sha256": "1cd16bc9f4f199c375da7cb9703336c6f6a2e166a55d7121ad1ed36e8d83b2db",
      "reader_unit_canonical_sha256": "4c25c092d41157b05a08e01c0f971e65c05d6551c05b1ce6fa01f30956890fa5",
      "reader_steps": 1
    },
    {
      "source_interface": "F5",
      "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Probability.GaussianHermiteFeatures.gaussianHermiteRidgeL2_ae",
      "kind": "theorem",
      "source_comparison": "accept",
      "module_comparison": "accept",
      "reader_exposition": "accept",
      "dependency_metadata": "accept",
      "reason": "The proof unfolds the actual toLp construction and applies its a.e. representative theorem, then eval_map_algebraMap reconciles the real polynomial evaluation with integer-polynomial aeval. It proves a.e. equality for each fixed j,w, not a pointwise representative identity or a simultaneous all-parameter full-measure set. The repaired dependency list now includes the directly used smoothness theorem.",
      "source_interface_canonical_sha256": "f296f8da0c8b59264156d0f89e6981a6453efb86a4c163b7fadabd5e76798f05",
      "reader_unit_canonical_sha256": "d568a03deae6909039f718adc3e4639068d086767210812f17200f7661ae5ed6",
      "reader_steps": 1
    },
    {
      "source_interface": "F6",
      "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Probability.GaussianHermiteFeatures.finiteGaussianHermiteRidgeL2_inner",
      "kind": "theorem",
      "source_comparison": "accept",
      "module_comparison": "accept",
      "reader_exposition": "accept",
      "dependency_metadata": "accept",
      "reason": "The proof uses L2.inner_def and the actual a.e. representatives to invoke the existing mixed Hermite integral theorem with both unit assumptions. Real bilinearity produces c_i*c_j; off-diagonal terms vanish and the diagonal becomes j!*c_j^2. Finite double-sum collapse handles empty support and degree zero without extra conditions. Signed correlations and endpoints are retained. No independence, orthogonality, coefficient positivity or normalization is assumed. This unit-direction identity is not extended to ambient nonunit directions.",
      "source_interface_canonical_sha256": "a34b569c8290971785468fe902ddaf891ef27dfc0646fa470dd2d52f9944d9de",
      "reader_unit_canonical_sha256": "2796c88cd867dd9f42d6d02e06182d0b0c8bf6fc9750030819eed9974462418c",
      "reader_steps": 3
    },
    {
      "source_interface": "F7",
      "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Probability.GaussianHermiteFeatures.finiteGaussianHermiteRidgeL2_contDiff",
      "kind": "theorem",
      "source_comparison": "accept",
      "module_comparison": "accept",
      "reader_exposition": "accept",
      "dependency_metadata": "accept",
      "reason": "ContDiff.sum and constant scalar multiplication apply to each degreewise C2 map. Finiteness alone replaces any series convergence condition. The theorem is on all of E and has no unit-vector premise.",
      "source_interface_canonical_sha256": "42a5010350ff7c31b7a5ac4a7e8d88a3db833ff13ec109a803ef7f1b39ace748",
      "reader_unit_canonical_sha256": "3f6cfa8d6615b406921dbca591ac1ed62ad99efe63f1dc34d3c26f06edc083c1",
      "reader_steps": 1
